From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryubing Android <ryubing-android@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] nce: identity-mapped address space window (guest VA == host pointer)

NCE executes guest code natively, so every guest pointer must be directly
dereferenceable by the host. Eden solves this by reserving one large window at
a random high address and enabling direct-mapped addressing (guest VA == host
pointer). Port that model:

- Ryujinx.Memory: MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE reserve-at-address (MemoryManagementUnix
  .ReserveAt, MemoryBlock.TryReserveAt), returned address verified.
- Ryujinx.Cpu: IdentityWindowPlacement (pure hint math: 2 MiB aligned base in
  [2^36, 2^39 - size)) and AddressSpace.TryCreateIdentityWindow (2^38 preferred,
  2^37 minimum, 64 attempts per size), mirroring HostMemory::ChooseVirtualBase.
- MemoryManagerHostNoMirror: identityMapped mode. Guest VAs are
  [WindowBase, WindowBase + WindowSize); page flags, page table and tracking are
  keyed by guest VA, only the MemoryBlock is addressed by window offset. No
  MemoryEhMeilleure is installed in this mode (the NCE SIGSEGV handler owns guest
  faults). Replaces the previous boost/peel dual-space heuristics entirely.
- VirtualMemoryManagerBase: ValidateAddress/ValidateAddressAndSize virtual.
- HostMapped/HostNoMirror Reprotect: real mprotect so SetProcessMemoryPermission
  (RX) makes guest .text executable (NCE instruction-fetches from it).

